commit a264ea7fb61f4d387d71927ff81d3cf6a4434d64
Author: Fabiano Silva <fabiano@freitassilva.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 07:48:15 2026 -0300

    fix(carwatch): anchor extract to classify's target vehicle, fix case mismatches
    
    Continuing the real-API extract run from the previous commit (11/13
    succeeded once the schema mismatch was fixed): the remaining 2 failures
    had two distinct real causes.
    
    1. A roundup article ("Every new car coming in 2026", covering dozens of
       vehicles) got approved by classify for one specific vehicle (Aion UT),
       but extract re-fetches the full page with no idea which vehicle
       classify meant -- it tried to describe the whole listicle, hit
       stop_reason="max_tokens" at the 1024-token ceiling, and produced
       unparseable JSON. Fix: pass classify's already-determined brand/model
       into extract's prompt as anchor context ("extract data ONLY for this
       vehicle"), and raise max_tokens 1024->1536 as a cheap safety margin
       (Anthropic bills tokens generated, not the ceiling, so this costs
       nothing on the normal ~300-500 token responses).
    
    2. drivetrain="AWD" (uppercase) against a lowercase-only literal
       ("fwd"/"rwd"/"awd"). Same class of case-mismatch could hit
       range_cycle (uppercase codes: WLTP/CLTC/EPA) and Price.status
       (lowercase) even though not yet observed for those -- added the same
       case-folding field_validator preemptively for all three.
    
    Verified against the real API 3x after the previous commit's fix (all
    OK) before this session ran the two straggler items through again;
    after this fix, both extracted successfully and the full 13/13 approved
    items are now real launch_events rows.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BsiqK4GWee7wjhH25RfiWM

